l01_26_type_resolution::fits::arrows_that_cover_only_across_two_parameters_are_refused_with_the_reason#040ee707	2:135	rejected	ArrowSplit	`p` does not take (((x: int, y: int) -> String) & ((x: bool, y: bool) -> String) & ((x: int, y: bool) -> String) & ((x: bool, y: int) -> String)): at `(x: Part1, y: Part1) -> String`, the arrow `(x: int, y: int) -> String` takes a part of more than one parameter, and arrows are combined only when they differ at one parameter: telling whether arrows that each split several parameters cover them all can take time exponential in the number of parameters, so the checker does not try; to repair it, write the arrows so that they differ at one parameter. /   Part1 stands for a part written more than once: /     type Part1 = int | bool;
